# Divisor of X-b on the rational function field

Theorem statement: `AlgebraicCurve.RationalFunctionField.ord_X_sub_C`
(`f9a2d286-c81a-519f-a515-e75850be890b`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `a29e81e9-cbd7-5100-a1a9-5ebfe9e17f8e`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Let $K$ be a field and $b \in K$. A place of $K(t) =$ `RatFunc K` over $K$ is, in this development,
a valuation subring of `RatFunc K` that contains the image of $K$, is not the whole field, and is a
principal ideal ring; for such a place $v$ and a function $f$, $v$`.ord`$f$ is $-\log$ of the value
of $f$ under the $\mathbb{Z}^{m0}$-valued valuation attached to the height-one point of the
valuation subring of $v$, i.e. the usual normalised order of vanishing. The assertion is that for
every place $v$ of `RatFunc K` over $K$, the order of the image of the polynomial $X - C\,b$ in
`RatFunc K` under the canonical map from $K[X]$ satisfies $$v.\mathrm{ord}\,(X-b) =
\bigl(\mathrm{single}\,(\mathrm{placeOfPoint}\,K\,b)\,1 +
\mathrm{single}\,(\mathrm{placeInfty}\,K)\,(-1)\bigr)(v),$$ the value at $v$ of the finitely
supported $\mathbb{Z}$-valued function which is the sum of the delta functions at two distinguished
places: `placeOfPoint K b`, the place coming from the height-one prime of $K[X]$ generated by the
irreducible polynomial $X - C\,b$, with coefficient $1$, and `placeInfty K`, the place whose
valuation subring is that of the infinite valuation of `RatFunc K`, with coefficient $-1$. Thus the
order is $1$ at the place of the point $b$, $-1$ at the place at infinity, and $0$ at every other
place.

This is the classical computation $\operatorname{div}(t-b) = (b) - (\infty)$ on $\mathbb{P}^1$,
stated place by place. It supports the identification of the places of $K(t)$ with the points of
$\mathbb{P}^1$ together with the point at infinity, and is used in the description of degree-zero
principal divisors on the rational function field and in the transfer of places under automorphisms
of $K(t)$.

